    "bottomLine": "The GNC product to grab when you cannot mix a shake, not the one to drink every day.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein / serving": "40 g (per GNC's listing)",
      "Calories": "About 190",
      "Sugar": "About 1 g",
      "Best for": "Convenience, travel"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "optimum-nutrition-gold-standard-100-whey",
    "name": "Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard 100% Whey",
    "brand": "Optimum Nutrition",
    "badge": "Alternative: Best Value Whey",
    "category": "Whey blend led by isolate",
    "description": "Gold Standard is the benchmark mainstream whey and the one AMP Wheybolic needs to beat on price. Per the label at the time of writing it delivers about 24 g of protein in roughly 120 calories per scoop, from a blend led by whey isolate, and Optimum Nutrition promotes Informed Choice certification on many flavors. That is almost the same scoop as Wheybolic Original's 25 g and 120 calories, so the choice comes down to price. In the large tubs on Amazon it is usually one of the cheapest per 25 g of protein among the major brands.",
    "pros": [
      "About 24 g of protein per scoop (label)",
      "Informed Choice on many flavors, per the brand",
